# Preview images offered on the landing page, in the order they appear there.
#
# One record per line, fields separated by tabs:
#
#   file<TAB>kind<TAB>description[<TAB>label]
#
# kind picks the icon: "disk" for a disk image, "video" for a recording.
# label is optional, the short name in the Download menu.
# The base URL is set by PDIMAGES_BASE_URL, and defaults to the one below.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

puredarwin-25.5-gpu.img	disk	The Argon desktop for x86_64 with AMD, Intel and NVIDIA GPU drivers, Wi-Fi and the built-in apps. UEFI, including 32-bit UEFI.	Desktop
puredarwin-25.5-gpu-sb.img	disk	The same desktop for machines with Secure Boot on. Enroll PUREDARWIN.cer once, see the Secure Boot page.	Desktop, Secure Boot
puredarwin-25.5-gpu-legacy.img	disk	The same desktop for machines that boot with a legacy BIOS.	Desktop, legacy BIOS
puredarwin-25.5-minimal.img	disk	A small x86_64 image that boots to a shell, the one used for most boot testing.	Minimal
puredarwin-arm64-rpi3-shell.mp4	video	Video from the 20.5 era: PureDarwin booting to a shell on a Raspberry Pi 3.
